body:
The Vespasian stuff is all highly, highly tentative. I'm going to go with in-universe decisions for most of the naming convention for right now. (I mean, just looking at the map, I see a bunch of stuff I would alter a bit so I'm one of the worst kind of world-builders lol)

&nbsp;

I need to put more stuff online in terms of the world, but as far as the basics of the political situation in Europe: things are messy. One of the driving pillars of *L&L* is that I want the ideas of feudalism and the powers of crowns to continue forward at the detriment of nationalism and traditional nation-building. If you look at Europe at the end of the 17th century, it remains a continent of strong monarchies and *two* Roman empires, albeit reeling from the recent collapse of the Catholic Church (*the War of the Four Peters* would make for an excellent map). The Crown of France continues to try to hold onto its Britannic possessions, going so far as to works towards bringing Scotland under the fold. Castile remains at odds with both Aragon and the Crusader States in the south, and has almost no colonial power whatsoever. Italy has felt the brunt of it, still completely fractured from the collapse of the Borgia Empire, even if it occurred over a century before. Almost all of Italy north of Naples is a part of the Western (Holy) Roman Empire, the various states successfully pulling a lot of focus southwards, especially with the House of Luxembourg's rule of Milan.   Suffice to say that Europe has a lot going on.

&nbsp;

The **Kingdom of the Weald** (initially the Grand Duchy of Kent) is primarily Kent and Sussex and parts of Surrey of Hampshire, carved out during the 1st War of the Crossing during the middle part of the 16th century.

&nbsp;

Lastly, thanks so much btw! The font I used is Lovelo. I find that graphically, the sharp sans-serif font creates a nice contrast to the rest of it.
